.TH PSVocabularyGetTokenID 3 2024-01-03 "PsyC 0.9.4" "PsyC Library Functions Manual"

.SH NAME
\fBPSVocabularyGetTokenID\fR \- Get the ID of the token from vocabulary

.SH LIBRARY
PsyC (-lpsyc)

.SH SYNOPSIS

.B
#include <psyc/dataset.h>

.I
int64_t  
.br
\fBPSVocabularyGetTokenID\fR(\fIPSVocabulary *vocabulary\fR, \fIchar *token\fR)
.SH DESCRIPTION
Get the ID of the token \fItoken\fR from vocabulary \fIvocabulary\fR.  

.SH RETURN VALUES
The numeric index (ID) of the token. If token is not found into \fIvocabulary\fR, the function will return \fIPS_TOKEN_NOT_FOUND\fR.
If \fIvocabulary\fR is \fINULL\fR or \fItoken\fR is \fINULL\fR, the function will return \fIPS_INVALID_TOKEN_ID\fR.

.SH SEE ALSO
psyc(1)
